DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  ppoossiixx__ooppeennpptt()  function opens an unused pseudoterminal master de‐
       vice, returning a file descriptor that can be used to refer to that de‐
       vice.

       The _f_l_a_g_s argument is a bit mask that ORs together zero or more of  the
       following flags:

       OO__RRDDWWRR Open  the  device  for both reading and writing.  It is usual to
              specify this flag.

       OO__NNOOCCTTTTYY
              Do not  make  this  device  the  controlling  terminal  for  the
              process.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, ppoossiixx__ooppeennpptt() returns a file descriptor (a nonnegative in‐
       teger)  which  is the lowest numbered unused file descriptor.  On fail‐
       ure, -1 is returned, and _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the error.

