HHIISSTTOORRYY
       glibc 2.2.1.  POSIX.1‐2001.

       It is part of the UNIX 98 pseudoterminal support (see ppttss(4)).

NNOOTTEESS
       Some older UNIX implementations that support System V (aka UNIX 98)
       pseudoterminals don’t have this function, but it can be easily
       implemented by opening the pseudoterminal multiplexor device:

           int
           posix_openpt(int flags)
           {
               return open("/dev/ptmx", flags);
           }

       Calling ppoossiixx__ooppeennpptt() creates a pathname for the corresponding
       pseudoterminal slave device.  The pathname of the slave device can be
       obtained using ppttssnnaammee(3).  The slave device pathname exists only as
       long as the master device is open.

